  "summary": "An op-ed by Mariya Genzel of Blue Turn Indivisible/Safety Over Surveillance coalition urging San Jose to suspend its Flock ALPR system after a San Jose police officer misused it to share a domestic-violence victim's location with her alleged abuser. The author argues guardrails cannot prevent surveillance creep, citing Mountain View's unauthorized access incident and other misuses nationally.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A San Jose police officer used the department's Flock system to share a woman's location with his cousin who was accused of abusing her.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Despite supposedly strict policies requiring the city to approve agencies individually, more than 250 unapproved agencies conducted roughly 600,000 searches of its Flock data in a single year.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "As a member of the Safety Over Surveillance coalition, I am asking San Jose to stop subjecting its residents to mass surveillance and immediately suspend the Flock cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
